# Reminder-only beat for demo step 2b: jump to definition with `v`.
#
# This beat never drives protolens — it only paces the presenter and shows
# short reminders in the script pane. The presenter navigates by hand.
# Advance each step with space or Enter.
#
# Invocation (from grehack2026.sh):
#   protolens --descriptor-set life.desc capture/000050-response.pb \
#       --script beats/jump

title: From a byte to its declaration

steps:
  - text: |
      Move the cursor onto a field whose type is a named message or enum
      (not a bare scalar).

      👋 Select such a field.

  - text: |
      Press `v`.

      protolens hands off to Neovim, opened at that type's declaration in
      the reconstructed .proto source — the SourceCodeInfo reproto
      synthesized, resolved against the proto/ stub beside life.desc.

      👋 Press `v`, look at the declaration, then come back.

  - text: |
      That is the point: schema recovery is not just a flat type list. We
      go from a byte on the wire to the exact line of reconstructed source
      that defines it, and back.

      👋 Press Enter to quit protolens.
